In article <2rp1ts$abp@news.bu.edu> kia@cs.bu.edu (Karl Asha) writes:
>This idea has brewed in my mind for years now. I wanted to know where
>people stand on the idea of nethack being a multi-player game. Is it
>possible, has it been done, is it wanted...I'm looking at a game
>that will be playable across the internet...lemme know what you think.


I could easily see a Nethack-LIKE multi-player game, and in fact I think
it's been tried before (see the Roguelike Games FAQ that gets posted here
occasionally)..  Nethack itself, though, really isn't cut out for it.
Treasure is too sparse, the quests and goal are too individualized, players
would have too much trouble cooperating with each other competitively, and
if they got to kill each other it would cause endless frustration.  Also,
though I don't agree with Jukka's assumption that players would have to wait
for each other's turns, simultaneous play would completely throw off the
interface and game code, and create lots of trouble in the program.

Still, look at the code and see if it's worth a try!  You could very
possibly adapt or invent an entirely new game, with the text-graphic
playability of Nethack but the excitement of multi-player combat games and
MUDs.

